# ── Recovered photography ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Neither of these belongs in git. Both are derived from the client's three PDF
# catalogues (248 MB, untracked at the repo root), and both are regenerable with
# `npm run slabs`. In production the images live in Cloudinary, uploaded once by
# `seedStones.js` — git is not the delivery mechanism.
#
#   public/slabs  cropped slabs, the seed's input
#   public/img    four WebP widths per slab, the old static pipeline's output,
#                 now referenced by nothing — the storefront asks the storage
#                 provider for the width it needs at render time
public/slabs
public/img

# TypeScript incremental build cache. Machine-local and regenerated on build.
*.tsbuildinfo

test-results
playwright-report

# Screenshots from `npm run visual-audit`. Regenerated on every run, and a
# few MB of PNGs per pass — a record of a moment, not part of the app.
audit-shots

.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
*.local
